.TH "VMINFO" "8" "June 2026" "" ""
.
.SH "NAME"
\fBvminfo\fR \-\- Vminfod Client Tool
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.
.nf
vminfo <SUBCOMMAND> [OPTIONS]
.
.fi
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBvminfo(8)\fR is a tool to interface with the \fBvminfod\fR service on a machine
using the exposed HTTP interface\.  It can be used for administrators to
determine service level health and status\.
.
.SH "SUBCOMMANDS"
\fBhelp\fR
    Print a help message and exit\.
.
.P
\fBping\fR
    Ping the server (GET /ping) and return the output with the appropriate exit
    status code set\.
.
.P
\fBstatus [\-j] [\-f]\fR
    Show server status (GET /status)\.  Supply \fB\-f\fR for "full" output (more
    internal details about vminfod\'s state) and \fB\-j\fR for JSON output\.
.
.P
\fBvms\fR
    Return a JSON array of all VMs known by vminfod (GET /vms)\. To use this
    programatically prefer \fBvmadm lookp \-j\fR\|\.
.
.P
\fBvm [uuid]\fR
    Return a JSON object for the VM uuid given known by vminfod (GET
    /vms/:uuid)\. To use this programatically prefer \fBvmadm get :uuid\fR\|\.
.
.P
\fBevents\fR
    Connect to the events stream (GET /events) and print events as they come in\.
    To use this programatically prefer \fBvmadm events\fR\|\.
.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
\fBvminfo ping\fR
    Check if the service is up\.
.
.P
\fBvminfo status \-f\fR
    Print full status\.
.
.SH "NOTES"
This tool should be used for interactive output only, and is not meant to
provide a stable interface to use for vminfod\.  If you are trying to interface
with \fBvminfod\fR use the \fBvmadm(8)\fR command (especially \fBvmadm events\fR) and, for
internal platform code, the \fBvminfod/client\fR Node\.js library\.
